About StarRez

StarRez is the global leader in student housing software, providing innovative solutions for on and off-campus housing management, resident wellness and experience, and revenue generation. Trusted by 1,400+ clients across 25+ countries, StarRez supports more than 4 million beds annually with its user-friendly, all-in-one platform, delivering seamless experiences for students and administrators. With offices in the United States, Australia, the UK, and India, StarRez blends the robust capabilities of a global organization with the personalized care and service of a trusted partner.

The Role   &nbsp;

As an UI/UX Designer, you’ll &nbsp;own the design of complex, data ‑ rich experiences that support decision ‑ making for administrators and improve clarity and usability across our platform. &nbsp;

You’ll &nbsp;work as a senior individual contributor within a cross ‑ functional product team :&nbsp; Design, Product, Engineering, bringing deep UI/UX&nbsp; expertise &nbsp;to your product area. While Product Management owns roadmap direction and prioritisation, you will play a critical role in informing decisions through research, design exploration, and user ‑ centred evidence, translating complexity into intuitive, accessible solutions. &nbsp;

This role sits within a newly established team focused on analytics, dashboards, and reporting, where&nbsp; you’ll &nbsp;elevate usability, interaction design, and data visualisation quality across&nbsp; StarRez &nbsp;products. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

What You Will Own &nbsp;

• Lead complex design initiatives from discovery through delivery, translating multi ‑ role, data ‑ heavy workflows into intuitive, scalable, and accessible experiences. &nbsp;

• Conduct and contribute to continuous discovery activities, including customer interviews, usability testing, and concept validation, surfacing insights that inform product decisions and reduce delivery risk. &nbsp;

• Partner with Product to support clear problem framing, hypotheses, and measures of success, using research, experimentation, and customer feedback to&nbsp;validate&nbsp;design decisions and iterate solutions. &nbsp;

• Work iteratively, shipping improvements in stages and refining designs based on real ‑ world usage, feedback, and&nbsp;observed&nbsp;outcomes. &nbsp;

• Elevate data visualisation quality across dashboards and reporting experiences, ensuring information is clear, meaningful, and usable for diverse audiences. &nbsp;

• Strengthen the broader product experience by contributing to our design system and embedding accessibility best practices (WCAG 2.2 AA) in collaboration with Engineering. &nbsp;

• Support stakeholder alignment through clear communication of UX decisions, improving usability and consistency through hands ‑ on critique, shared UI/UX patterns, and informal mentorship. &nbsp;

• Actively&nbsp;leverage&nbsp;AI ‑ powered tools and workflows within the design practice to accelerate exploration, iteration, and problem ‑ solving.  &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Required Qualifications &nbsp;

• 5+ years of experience designing complex SaaS or B2B digital products. &nbsp;

• Strong experience designing&nbsp;data ‑ rich&nbsp;interfaces, including dashboards, reporting tools, or complex operational systems.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience contributing to measurable product or business impact through improved usability, efficiency, or user satisfaction. &nbsp;

• Strong systems thinking and experience working across interconnected workflows or multi-role platforms. &nbsp;

• Proficiency&nbsp;in interaction design, information architecture, and high-fidelity execution. &nbsp;

• Experience leading discovery efforts and synthesizing insights into actionable product decisions. &nbsp;

• Strong communication&nbsp;skills and the ability to articulate design rationale clearly to cross-functional stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Experience partnering closely with Engineering to ensure high-quality implementation. &nbsp;

Company Overview

Metrea delivers effects-as-a-service to national security partners across five domains and more than a dozen mission areas. These include airborne ISR, electronic warfare, secure communications, aerial refueling, special air missions, aerial firefighting, and advanced simulation. We own the whole stack: designing, building, and operating turnkey capabilities that give our partners decisive, asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats.

Our operating model is built around three interlocking pillars. The Support Groups provide a global shared-service - spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement. This frees up our Core Groups, who develop and own mission capabilities end-to-end, to focus entirely on delivery. The Market Groups apply a regional lens, ensuring that our agile and adaptable capabilities remain aligned to the wicked problems that matter most to our partners across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific.

At the heart of our model is a simple but powerful idea: be a true partner with skin in the game. Our partners need effects, not just equipment. By owning the full stack - from the lab to the field - we are able to drive a continuous cycle of innovation that keeps our partners ahead. It's a fast-moving, intellectually demanding environment where talented people are given real responsibility, work on problems that matter, and contribute to an enterprise that is growing quickly and deliberately.

Headquartered in Washington, DC, with facilities across the United States, the United Kingdom, as well as Continental Europe and Asia-Pacific.

Group&nbsp;Overview

Metrea is actively building its presence in Australia as part of a deliberate, globally coordinated expansion into the Asia-Pacific region. Our Asia-Pacific Market Group, headquartered in Brisbane with an additional office in Perth, is the enterprise's dedicated regional interface connecting Australia's national security community with Metrea's full suite of capabilities across three core domains: Aerospace, Electromagnetic &amp; Cyber, and Digital &amp; Synthetic. Metrea is now bringing that same depth of mission expertise and proven operating model to Australia.&nbsp;

Underpinning these capabilities is a global network of Support Groups spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement - ensuring that as we grow in Australia, we do so with the full weight of an established global enterprise behind us.&nbsp;

Metrea's solutions are built for elegance: effective, efficient, and evolving - enabling our partners to scale capacity and achieve asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats. &nbsp;

Position Summary

This is a high-impact, strategic role responsible for shaping and delivering end-to-end category, sourcing and Australian Industry Capability strategies across multiple operational and programmatic requirements. You will work closely with suppliers, Australian Industry partners, and internal stakeholders to establish sourcing strategies, supplier networks, local capability pathways and commercial frameworks that ensure the right products and services are available at the right quality, cost, and time while strengthening Australian industry participation, ethical sourcing, innovation and supply chain resilience. embedding sustainability, ethical sourcing, innovation, and supply chain resilience. &nbsp;

This is an outstanding opportunity for an experienced procurement and strategic sourcing professional with strong supplier management, negotiation and industry engagement capabilities to help build and enhance Metrea's regional procurement capability across Australia and the Asia-Pacific region while delivering meaningful commercial outcomes and advancing global procurement standards. &nbsp;

In this role, you will lead the development and execution of category strategies that support a resilient, compliant, low-risk, and high-performing supply chain.

